#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# is_odd

#% text
# `is_odd(n)` gives `true` when `n` is an odd integer, else `false`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Anything that is not an explicit integer gives `false`: a symbol, a closed form, a machine real such as `3.0`, a string (as for `is_even`, `is_integer` and `is_prime`).

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
is_odd(7)
#% output
#= true

#% cell
is_odd(4)
#% output
#= false

#% cell
is_odd(-3)
#% output
#= true

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Count the odd numbers in a list:

#% cell
count_if(range(20), is_odd)
#% output
#= 10

#% subsection
# Possible issues

#% text
# A machine real is not an integer, even when it has no fractional part:

#% cell
is_odd(3.0)
#% output
#= false

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `is_even`, `mod`, `is_integer`
